"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[94789],{194789:e=>{e.exports="# How to configure gold table\n\nGold tables are built from silver data. Field definitions use the same FieldSpec types as silver (`from`, `expr`, `literal`, etc.).\n\n**Important:** We may override fields in gold tables using `addFields` or `omitFields`. However, adding or removing fields in **existing** gold tables (whether preset or custom) is **not recommended**, since a gold table’s schema is fixed at creation and cannot be changed later.\n\n---\n\n## Quick reference: gold paths\n\n- **New gold table (add):** `gold.presetOverrides.addTables[]` → `name`, `sourceTable`, `fields`, optional `filter`, `postFilter`.\n- **Existing preset gold (modify):** `gold.presetOverrides.modifyTables[]` → `name`, `sourceTable`, then `filter`/`postFilter` or (if necessary) `omitFields`/`addFields`. Prefer filtering over schema changes.\n\n**Matching:** Overrides match by **name** (gold table) and **sourceTable** (preset’s `input`). Set both when modifying a preset gold table.\n\n**How to update a preset field (gold):** Same mechanism as silver: (1) Add the field name to `omitFields`. (2) Add a field with the same name in `addFields` with the new definition.\n\n---\n\n## Examples: gold\n\n### Example: New gold table (addTables) — preferred\n\nCreate a gold table that does not exist in the preset. Set `name`, `sourceTable` (silver table to read from), and `fields`. Include a `time` column (TIMESTAMP).\n\n**User Request:** \"Create a gold table for authentication events from auth_events_silver\"\n\n```yaml\ngold:\n  presetOverrides:\n    addTables:\n      - name: auth_events_gold\n        sourceTable: auth_events_silver\n        filter: \"status = 'success'\"\n        fields:\n          - name: time\n            from: event_time\n          - name: user_id\n            from: user_id\n          - name: event_type\n            literal: 'authentication'\n```\n\n### Example: Filtering (gold)\n\nApply pre- or post-filters when building the gold table.\n\n```yaml\ngold:\n  presetOverrides:\n    modifyTables:\n      - name: security_findings_gold\n        sourceTable: security_logs_silver\n        filter: \"status = 'success'\"\n# postFilter: after field transforms\n#   postFilter: 'is_valid = true AND time IS NOT NULL'\n```\n\n### Example: Override time column (omit + add)\n\nUse only when the preset’s time column must be replaced (e.g. use `event_time` instead of default). Omit the preset field, then add the same name in `addFields`.\n\n```yaml\ngold:\n  presetOverrides:\n    modifyTables:\n      - name: security_findings_gold\n        sourceTable: security_logs_silver\n        omitFields: ['time']\n        addFields:\n          - name: time\n            from: event_time\n```\n\n### Example: Add or remove field on existing table (discouraged)\n\nIf you must add or remove a field on an existing gold table:\n\n**Add field:** Add a `modifyTables` entry with `name`, `sourceTable`, and `addFields`.\n\n**Remove field:** Add the field name to `omitFields` in the same entry.\n\n```yaml\n# Add field (discouraged)\nmodifyTables:\n  - name: <gold_table_name>\n    sourceTable: <silver_table_name>\n    addFields:\n      - name: finding_severity_label\n        expr: \"CASE WHEN severity >= 4 THEN 'High' WHEN severity >= 2 THEN 'Medium' ELSE 'Low' END\"\n\n# Remove field (discouraged)\n#   omitFields: ['internal_metadata']\n```\n\n---\n\n## Key concepts (gold)\n\n- **addTables** — For new gold tables. You define the full `fields` list. `sourceTable` must be an existing silver table name.\n- **modifyTables** — For existing preset gold tables. Match by `name` + `sourceTable`. Prefer changing `filter`/`postFilter`; avoid changing schema (add/remove fields) unless necessary.\n- **Time column** — Every gold table must have a `time` column (TIMESTAMP). In addTables, include it in `fields`. If you omit it in modifyTables, re-add it in `addFields`.\n\n---\n\n## Common patterns: gold\n\n**New gold table:**\n\n```yaml\ngold:\n  presetOverrides:\n    addTables:\n      - name: summary_gold\n        sourceTable: events_silver\n        fields:\n          - name: time\n            from: event_time\n          - name: event_type\n            from: event_type\n```\n\n**Override time column on existing gold:**\n\n```yaml\nmodifyTables:\n  - name: <gold_table_name>\n    sourceTable: <silver_table_name>\n    omitFields: ['time']\n    addFields:\n      - name: time\n        from: event_time\n```\n\n---\n\n## Gold-specific mistakes to avoid\n\n- **Adding/removing fields on existing gold tables** — Discouraged; can break consumers.\n- **Wrong or missing sourceTable** — Must match the preset’s `input` (modifyTables) or an existing silver table (addTables).\n- **Using modifyTables for a new gold table** — Use `addTables` when the gold table doesn’t exist in the preset.\n- **Omitting time without re-adding** — Gold requires a `time` column; if you omit it, add it back in `addFields`.\n- **Referencing non-existent silver columns** — Verify silver schema when defining `fields` or `addFields`.\n"}}]);
